{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0443ea8bc98c677a04ef9d672abba7b476009e22d2ca8bc38dd7537f90dbb324"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The orchestration section lists LangChain, LlamaIndex, Haystack, DSPy, Semantic Kernel, Langflow, Flowise, Promptflow, and Dify."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0f633175579acb0ccea8dedb6b11743953b3d803d968b9fe83a4fe57343187d6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The catalog includes PDF extraction tools (Docling, pdfplumber, PyMuPDF, Camelot, Unstructured, Llama Parse, etc.) and web scraping tools (Firecrawl, Scrapy, Playwright, Crawl4AI, etc.)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5658e724addacb263f01eaf2057895d773c9ebde76c9d52d7d5d923abdd5da12"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sections on LLM inference and serving list vLLM, TensorRT-LLM, WebLLM, Ollama, llama.cpp, LocalAI, LiteLLM, and inference platforms like Modal, Replicate, Groq, and OpenRouter."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7b2dd1fe64ff95592c6f0f4931cb1ca924fa210cd7f2833e26221f896de4b562"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are instructed to fork the repository, create a feature branch, add their contribution, and submit a pull request."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8c0e4c55cd5986e656e0c1f24f1942119e1e7b9e09343ada2521e47a6e25fd31"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The evaluation and testing section lists OpenAI Evals, Ragas, Opik, Phoenix, DeepEval, TruLens, UpTrain, Giskard, Weave, Lighteval, and Langfuse."},{"claim_ids":["clm_915d8e1c7adb799e5fc43d96388cb50e4e3ef97514b08a25900c0cc1ad3c59ac"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent frameworks section lists Google's ADK, AutoGen, CrewAI, LangGraph, AgentOps, Swarm, Agency Swarm, Auto-GPT, and BabyAGI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9cfdc105f0a645314c6b800fd47581e93a8c8990e60b776aea7367297fab2fcc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is a curated list of 100+ libraries and frameworks for AI engineers building with LLMs, including tools, templates, and reference implementations."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c8b1001359f55823171c406da39b94e6bfa83b55d2cef1d9764440cf8fee65a3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository is MIT licensed, per the license badge in the README."},{"claim_ids":["clm_df069b04ae28adfbe05760a98a0c0c6a68a9546bc3caa996123776a333e335a0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The vector databases section lists tools such as Pinecone, Weaviate, Qdrant, Chroma, Milvus, FAISS, Deep Lake, and Vectara with language and license details."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e1b0e78f002b6efc20045bc227251c3d29844c6636791f0f0c46adeeeb33550e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each tool entry is presented in a table with columns for tool name, description, language, and license; inference platforms use pricing and feature columns instead."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f1f68660a5c170ba4898ccc143401b33f09ce23b540671fd4ee86d40d01c5c85"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The catalog is organized into sections covering vector databases, orchestration, RAG, evaluation, model management, web scraping, agent frameworks, LLM optimization, inference, safety, and structured generation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f2067e36714847e0a5d3af3b5a926ae003b5c1e59e33f7991d4e81fe2accc206"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contribution guidelines ask for quality over quantity, production-ready tools, clear documentation with usage examples, and actively maintained tools."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0443ea8bc98c677a04ef9d672abba7b476009e22d2ca8bc38dd7537f90dbb324","clm_0f633175579acb0ccea8dedb6b11743953b3d803d968b9fe83a4fe57343187d6","clm_5658e724addacb263f01eaf2057895d773c9ebde76c9d52d7d5d923abdd5da12","clm_7b2dd1fe64ff95592c6f0f4931cb1ca924fa210cd7f2833e26221f896de4b562","clm_8c0e4c55cd5986e656e0c1f24f1942119e1e7b9e09343ada2521e47a6e25fd31","clm_915d8e1c7adb799e5fc43d96388cb50e4e3ef97514b08a25900c0cc1ad3c59ac","clm_9cfdc105f0a645314c6b800fd47581e93a8c8990e60b776aea7367297fab2fcc","clm_c8b1001359f55823171c406da39b94e6bfa83b55d2cef1d9764440cf8fee65a3","clm_df069b04ae28adfbe05760a98a0c0c6a68a9546bc3caa9961